() Tj T*
(THE RISE OF ?PEASANTISM.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The awful famine which has lately been raging over an area as large) Tj T*
(as the territory of the _Dreibund_, and inhabited by a population as) Tj T*
(numerous as that of the ?allied Republic,? has called the attention) Tj T*
(of the whole civilized world to the condition of the starving Russian) Tj T*
(peasant. A movement has been set on foot in this country to relieve) Tj T*
(the hard need of the sufferers. This has induced me to think that it) Tj T*
(would perhaps not be without some interest for the American student) Tj T*
(of economics to cast a glance at the rural conditions which have) Tj T*
(finally resulted in that tremendous calamity. I felt bound to improve) Tj T*
(the opportunity of having been educated in Russia, by introducing) Tj T*
(the American reader to some one portion of the vast Russian economic) Tj T*
(literature which, because of the language, remains as yet completely) Tj T*
(unknown to the scientific world at large.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Russians by education, though not by ethnical descent, who, in spite) Tj T*
(of having identified themselves with the cause of the Russian people,) Tj T*
(are now denied the honorable title of ?Russian,? may find consolation) Tj T*
(in the fact that the first investigator of Russian history \(Schlözer\),) Tj T*
(the first grammarian who scientifically elaborated the laws of Russian) Tj T*
