(grammar, our Brown \(Vostokoff = von Osteneck\), the best, if not the) Tj T*
(first Russian lexicographer, our Webster \(Dahl\), and finally the man) Tj T*
(who, it may be said, discovered for the Russian public the Russian) Tj T*
(village community, the _mir_ \(Freiherr August von Haxthausen\), were all) Tj T*
(of foreign birth.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The last named discovery was destined to play a prominent part in) Tj T*
(the subsequent political history of Russia. Agrarian communism,) Tj T*
(spread throughout a vast country during an age of extreme economic) Tj T*
(individualism, when the last traces of such a form of possession were) Tj T*
(deeply buried in the past of European nations, gave rise for years to) Tj T*
(an erroneous theory both in Russia and in Western Europe, _viz_: that) Tj T*
(this was a specifically Russian or Slavic institution. In Russia it) Tj T*
(contributed greatly towards drawing the line between the two parties of) Tj T*
(the Russian educated class in ?the epoch of the forties,? between the) Tj T*
(?occidentalists? \(_zapadniki_\) and the ?slavophiles.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The latter regarded the village community as being, with autocracy and) Tj T*
(orthodoxy, an emanation of the Russian ?national spirit.? These three) Tj T*
(institutions were predestined in their belief to prevent Holy Russ from) Tj T*
(entering upon the impious ways of the ?rotten West,? with its class) Tj T*
(antagonism, extremes of luxury and poverty, intestinal discords and) Tj T*
(civil wars.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Precisely for the same reasons, considering the village community) Tj T*
(as an integral part of the prevailing system of paternalism, the) Tj T*
(?occidentalists,? opposed to autocracy and orthodoxy, strove for the) Tj T*
(abolition of the _mir_ as well as of bond serfdom.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The archaic communism of the _mir_ appeared to them to stand in acute) Tj T*
(contradiction to Western liberalism or individualism. The ?epoch of) Tj T*
(emancipation,? however, that came to realize the aspirations of the) Tj T*
(occidentalists, brought about a fundamental change of public opinion in) Tj T*
(regard to the village community.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The intellectual development in Russia was ever going on under the) Tj T*
(steady influence of Western ideas. The ?epoch of the forties? coincided) Tj T*
(with the era during which socialistic and communistic ideas were in) Tj T*
(full blast throughout France. Thanks to the many Russian tourists) Tj T*
(and students who became imbued with these ideas during their sojourn) Tj T*
(in Paris, socialism, towards the end of ?the forties,? attained no) Tj T*
(inconsiderable popularity among the educated class in Russia. Not to) Tj T*
(speak of Herzen or Bakunin--who were at that time closely affiliated) Tj T*
(with Proudhon, Karl Marx and other prominent representatives of the) Tj T*
(social movements of the day--Belinsky, who was the foremost Russian) Tj T*
(critic and publicist, equally renowned among all parties \(except,) Tj T*
(of course, the bureaucratic party\), became in his latter years a) Tj T*
(socialist. ?Secret circles,? or, as they would be called in this) Tj T*
(country, debating clubs, swarmed in every large centre of intellectual) Tj T*
(culture. Among the young men connected with this movement, there was) Tj T*
(one who was later on to play a part of extraordinary importance in) Tj T*
(Russian history; this was _Nicholas Gavrielovitch Tchernyshefsky_.) Tj T*
