() Tj T*
(The influence of Tchernyshefsky upon the development of Russia) Tj T*
(was far wider, and far more many-sided, than might be supposed.) Tj T*
(Philosophy, ethics, æsthetics, criticism, political economy, politics,) Tj T*
(fiction:--these were the various fields of his activity; and everywhere) Tj T*
(his ideas determined the course of further development. It would) Tj T*
(require the elaborate study of a scholar to truly represent the) Tj T*
(historical value of Tchernyshefsky, who can justly be called the father) Tj T*
(of Russian Nihilism.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Nihilism was entirely misunderstood in Western countries. It will,) Tj T*
(perhaps, appear somewhat surprising to an English reader to learn that) Tj T*
(Jeremy Bentham?s doctrine of utilitarianism offered the philosophical) Tj T*
(foundation of Nihilism. The latter was in reality nothing but an) Tj T*
(attempt to construct socialism upon the basis of individual utility.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The village community, seen in the light of Nihilism, must evidently) Tj T*
(have presented quite a different aspect from that which it presented to) Tj T*
(both the slavophiles and the occidentalists of the preceding epoch. The) Tj T*
(first article of Tchernyshefsky upon the village community was written) Tj T*
(in 1857, on the eve of the emancipation of the peasants, and was in the) Tj T*
(form of a criticism on the papers that had appeared in the slavophile) Tj T*
(magazine _Russkaya Beseda_. Tchernyshefsky, though apparently an) Tj T*
(?occidentalist,? sided with the slavophiles, and in a series of) Tj T*
(brilliant articles laid down the basis of the so-called ?peasantism?) Tj T*
(\(_narodnitchestvo_\) which since then, and until quite recently, has) Tj T*
(constituted the common ground of all liberal and radical aspirations in) Tj T*
(Russia, however greatly they may have differed upon other questions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Must Russian development of historical necessity follow in the tracks) Tj T*
(of Western Europe? Cannot Russia benefit by the lessons taught by the) Tj T*
(history of Western nations, and find out some new way of her own to) Tj T*
(avoid that evil of pauperism which necessarily accompanies private) Tj T*
(enterprise in production??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These were the questions raised by Tchernyshefsky. Taking as a basis) Tj T*
(Hegel?s famous triad, he showed that Western Europe went from State) Tj T*
(regulation to individualism and _laissez-faire_, and now was entering) Tj T*
(upon a new path which tended toward coöperation and social regulation) Tj T*
(of economic phenomena. Why then should Russia pass through the) Tj T*
(intermediate phase, since she already possessed a national institution) Tj T*
(which permeated the whole economic life of the people, and embodied) Tj T*
(the principles of coöperation? The individualistic French farmer must) Tj T*
(inevitably succumb in the war of competition with the large landholder,) Tj T*
(for the latter is in a position to utilize all new agricultural) Tj T*
(improvements, while the former lacks all means of combination with his) Tj T*
(neighbors. On the other hand, supposing that the time has come for the) Tj T*
(introduction of improved machinery into Russian agriculture, would) Tj T*
(it require any revolution in the social relations prevailing in the) Tj T*
(Russian village? Not in the least; the land belongs to the community,) Tj T*
(and not to the individual; the forms of distribution of land are) Tj T*
(very various, and admit, not infrequently, even of collective mowing) Tj T*
ET
