(In the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries the present _gubernias_ of) Tj T*
(Middle Russia formed the boundaries of Muscovy adjoining the dominions) Tj T*
(of the Porte and the military Republic of Little Russia. To defend) Tj T*
(the borders of the state a kind of national militia, or yeomanry, was) Tj T*
(settled along the frontiers. As usual, it was granted land in fee. The) Tj T*
(gradual transformation of fee into patrimony by force of legislation) Tj T*
(did not, however, concern this class of tenants in fee, as they did) Tj T*
(not count among the gentry. Nevertheless, the process went on, thanks) Tj T*
(to the natural play of economic forces. Mr. Pankeyeff, in his essay) Tj T*
(on the subject, does not show us the causes of the frequent sales of) Tj T*
(small fees during the eighteenth century. As the times coincided with) Tj T*
(the period during which the resources of the country were strained to) Tj T*
(the utmost in order to keep up the aggressive annexation policy of the) Tj T*
(Empire, it seems very probable that this mobility of the land belonging) Tj T*
(to the yeomen \(_odnodvortzy_, as they were designated after 1719\) was) Tj T*
