(under agrarian communism[26], is 458,000 poods[27], and this has to be) Tj T*
(distributed among 83,079 head of large cattle[28]. This makes on an) Tj T*
(average 5½ _poods_, _i. e._ 200 pounds to every head for the Russian) Tj T*
(winter, lasting at least half a year. In other words, there is about) Tj T*
(_one pound of hay a day_ for every head of cattle.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Nor is the condition any better in the summer, since the pastures,) Tj T*
(where there are any, are very scanty; and this is due to conversion) Tj T*
(of pasture into arable land, as already mentioned, as well as into) Tj T*
(homesteads for the increased population. This reduces to a paltry) Tj T*
(figure the number of cattle raised by the peasants.[29] Two working) Tj T*
(horses to a farm can hardly be considered as representing, even for) Tj T*
(Russian agriculture, a particularly high standard. The actual extent) Tj T*
(to which stock-breeding is carried on by the peasants falls below even) Tj T*
(this minimum, save among the 415 quarterly proprietors in the Ranenburg) Tj T*
(district, who are a kind of peasant ?four hundred? in their own way,) Tj T*
(owing to the extent of allotted land that they own.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The depressed condition of stock-breeding reacts in its turn upon) Tj T*
(agriculture. Apart from this there is another universal cause that) Tj T*
(diverts the cattle manure from its natural use. I refer to the lack of) Tj T*
(woods.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(With respect to possession of forests, so necessary in a climate like) Tj T*
(Russia, most of the state peasants were originally in a privileged) Tj T*
(condition, compared with the former serfs, to whom, as a rule,) Tj T*
(no woodland at all was allotted.[30] However, time has effaced) Tj T*
(all distinction between the privileged communities and those less) Tj T*
(fortunate. Of the former forests there remain at present only shrubs,) Tj T*
(and young bushes, of no practical value. State peasant and former) Tj T*
(serf are equally dominated by the want of fuel, a want which must be) Tj T*
(satisfied with the only burning material at hand, _viz_: with dung. In) Tj T*
(many a community this precludes the fertilizing of the soil altogether;) Tj T*
(in a great many others it is but the land next to the homestead that) Tj T*
(is manured, and the poorest among the peasants have no manure at all) Tj T*
(worth carrying to their fields. It is needless to speak of the extent) Tj T*
