(That there is one part of the payments to the landlord which is in) Tj T*
(reality nothing but a redemption tax for the person of the serf,[45]) Tj T*
(appears clear from the comparison between the amount of rent paid by) Tj T*
(the former State peasant to the treasury, and that of the taille paid) Tj T*
(by the ?temporary obligor? to his master, since in neither is any) Tj T*
(portion set apart for redemption of the land. And the amount of taille) Tj T*
(paid is made the basis for the amortization.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the other hand, the least amount in taxes is paid by those among) Tj T*
(the former serfs who have already redeemed their lots \(?absolute) Tj T*
(proprietors?\) or who received the so-called donated lots, _i. e._, the) Tj T*
(least is levied from those who are free from the obligation to their) Tj T*
(former masters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Here, however, we are again face to face with the characteristic) Tj T*
(feature of the Russian financial system: the ?absolute proprietor,? who) Tj T*
(owns from six to ten times as much land as the donee, and who breeds) Tj T*
(more than twice as much stock as the latter, is taxed from four to) Tj T*
(eight times less upon every acre. It would be absurd to suspect even) Tj T*
(a Russian financial administration of the intention to overtax the) Tj T*
(neediest while relieving the burdens of the better-off. Yet this is the) Tj T*
(necessary result of a financial system which belongs to a different) Tj T*
(historical epoch, and has survived the overthrow of its economic) Tj T*
(foundations through a social revolution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Let us take as a unit every male of the revision, \(_i. e._, the) Tj T*
(official unit of taxation\); let us then compare with one another) Tj T*
(the assessments levied upon both exceptional classes of absolute) Tj T*
(proprietors and donees, on the one hand, and let us again compare with) Tj T*
(each other the assessments levied upon the remaining classes of the) Tj T*
(peasantry. We shall see that every male is taxed on the whole at an) Tj T*
(approximately uniform rate. This is the usual system of taxation in) Tj T*
(every primitive state, where land is in abundance and human labor is) Tj T*
(the main source of wealth. The labor powers of men being approximately) Tj T*
(equal, assessment _per capita_ insures a rude equity in taxation.) Tj T*
(But after the reforms of 1861 and 1866, which added new and sharp) Tj T*
(distinctions to those already in existence among the peasantry,) Tj T*
