(taxation _per capita_ became a power that accentuated the social) Tj T*
(inequalities, and hastened, through its extortion, the ruin of the) Tj T*
(feeble.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Indebtedness of landed property is the inclined plane usually) Tj T*
(leading toward expropriation of the small farmer, as well as of the) Tj T*
(aristocratic landlord. In Russia the three minor subdivisions of the) Tj T*
(peasantry, viz. the ?absolute proprietors,? the ?donees? and the) Tj T*
(?quarterly possessors,? are the only ones who enjoy the title of) Tj T*
(property in their land, and consequently they alone are in a position) Tj T*
(to mortgage to private persons. The bulk of the peasantry[46] have no) Tj T*
(right of alienating their plots. Chronic indebtedness upon the latter) Tj T*
(takes, therefore, as its only possible form that of arrears in taxes,) Tj T*
(which is precisely the sore place of the Russian administration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The amount of ?arrears? due by the peasants to the treasury is) Tj T*
(represented by no inconsiderable figure, as may be seen from the) Tj T*
