(the former state peasant, the _taille_ or the redemption tax imposed) Tj T*
(upon the former serf. In other words, one-third of the former State) Tj T*
(peasants, and three-eighths of the former serfs, are unable to bear) Tj T*
(the fee levied for the use of their land.[48] Finally, this fact) Tj T*
(attracted the attention of the central government, and in 1882, the) Tj T*
(_zemstvos_ were required by the Minister of the Interior to report) Tj T*
(upon ?the communities in which husbandry had fallen into ultimate) Tj T*
(destitution,?[49] and a relief in the amount of the redemption tax was) Tj T*
(desirable. The committee elected by the _zemstvo_ of the district of) Tj T*
(Ryazañ applied, as we learn, to the Reports of the Statistical Bureau.) Tj T*
(The same could hardly be done for the districts under consideration,) Tj T*
(since the Reports were subsequently proscribed by the _zemstvo_ of) Tj T*
(the _gubernia_ of Ryazañ.[50] If the Reports were taken into account,) Tj T*
(all the above three-eighths of the former serfs would perhaps have) Tj T*
(to be classed among those whose husbandry ?has fallen into ultimate) Tj T*
(destitution,? since above one-fourth owed to the treasury 20.10 rubles,) Tj T*
(and one-ninth above 34 ruble to an average household. This one-ninth) Tj T*
(was in chronic arrears of from one to two annual instalments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Whatever may be the absolute amount of the arrears, the point is that) Tj T*
(they bear upon the peasant?s live stock, which is the only valuable) Tj T*
(part of his movable property, and is consequently the first to be taken) Tj T*
(hold of by the auctioneer. Arrears in taxes are, therefore, a constant) Tj T*
(threat to the very existence of the peasant?s farming.[51]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Moreover they bind the peasant to the spot, and thus restrict the) Tj T*
(market for his labor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This, however, is only an evil of the transitional epoch. A change of) Tj T*
(great moment has taken place in so short a period as the ten years) Tj T*
(which separate the census of the _zemstvo_ from the investigations of) Tj T*
(the above mentioned Commissions of the central government.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Overtaxation has been swallowed up in the increase in value of) Tj T*
(the land. The rent of the peasant?s plot in both districts of the) Tj T*
(_gubernia_ of Ryazañ exceeds the taxes by from one to three rubles) Tj T*
(\(_i. e._ the taxes absorb, in an average, from 78 to 91 per cent. of) Tj T*
(the rent.\)[52] Though rise of rent is by no means a blessing for the) Tj T*
(Russian peasant, partly tenant, partly agricultural laborer as he is,) Tj T*
(yet the benefit he gains as taxpayer is the possibility of disposing) Tj T*
(of his labor by leasing his plot to any one willing to pay the taxes) Tj T*
(thereon.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus the old question of chronic arrears is to-day easy to be settled) Tj T*
(through public sale of the peasant?s stock. Flogging as a measure) Tj T*
(of financial policy can be dispensed with, so far at least as the) Tj T*
(insolvent debtor is concerned; for the taxes are secured by the land,) Tj T*
(over and above the body of the taxpayer.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus economic evolution has loosened the legal bonds which formerly) Tj T*
ET
