(agreements are the rarest exception. The latter form is, however,) Tj T*
(likely to keep pace with the development of money economy in rural) Tj T*
(relations. So long as the easement is granted in consideration of a) Tj T*
(certain amount of farm work to be done, \(and this is now the ordinary) Tj T*
(rule\), it is to the landlord?s advantage to secure the collective) Tj T*
(labor of a whole community at once, instead of entering into a special) Tj T*
(agreement with each peasant for a small service. The fulfilment of) Tj T*
(the obligation is secured by the joint suretyship of the community,) Tj T*
(while to sue each peasant for failure to perform two or three days?) Tj T*
(work would be far too troublesome. It certainly matters little to the) Tj T*
(landlord, how the labor is distributed among the several members of the) Tj T*
(community, and it was but in 12 cases out of 105 that the agreement was) Tj T*
(made for so much work to be done _per_ head. On the other hand payment) Tj T*
(was stipulated for at so much _per_ head in 14 out of 37 cases, in) Tj T*
(which the transaction was one of money. But as soon as the agreement) Tj T*
(is made in this form, the householders can act individually as well as) Tj T*
(through the _mir_, and this was in reality the case in 6 communities) Tj T*
(out of the 156, the peasants managing to get their cattle counted as) Tj T*
(part of the landlord?s flock.) Tj T*
