(The patriarchal custom of division of the product itself between) Tj T*
(landlord and tenant \(_métayage_\) has now become about entirely) Tj T*
(obsolete, and is now to be found only in combination with extra) Tj T*
(payments in money. Forced labor on the part of the peasant for the) Tj T*
(benefit of the landlord continued in use. Abolished by law, it has) Tj T*
(been upheld until to-day, through the economic pressure of the need of) Tj T*
(land. The free tenant was compelled to bind himself to do a certain) Tj T*
(amount of work for the landlord. If he failed in this he could not get) Tj T*
(the opportunity of renting land. Pecuniary agreements were in vogue on) Tj T*
(those estates alone, whose owners did not care for farming.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The economic tendency of the time, however, is toward money economy) Tj T*
(and ?free contract.?[69] As in the matter of taxation, the change is) Tj T*
(brought about by the rise of rent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the one hand, the amount of work done by the tenant for the landlord) Tj T*
(has enormously increased, thereby diminishing the demand for compulsory) Tj T*
(labor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the other hand, whenever the rent is to be paid in cash, at least) Tj T*
(one part must be advanced in the spring, _i. e._ at a time when most of) Tj T*
(the peasants are short of money. Moreover, the extraordinarily heavy) Tj T*
(rents exacted have made the leasing of land a very hazardous business;) Tj T*
(one bad yield is sufficient to upset all the tenant?s calculations,) Tj T*
(and to throw him into insolvency.[70] The circle of tenants who can) Tj T*
(pay their rents in cash has thus been reduced to the ?stronger?) Tj T*
(householders.[71] The natural consequence was increased offers of farm) Tj T*
(labor in exchange for land, on the part of those who could not afford) Tj T*
(to lay out ready money.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus in the process of the economic evolution, compulsory labor becomes) Tj T*
(obsolete. It was only in the minority of cases that the promise of) Tj T*
(labor was required as an essential part of the rental agreement, and) Tj T*
(even then it was only in exceptional cases that farm work was to be) Tj T*
(performed for the full amount of the rent. Generally only a part of the) Tj T*
(latter was to be covered through labor; the rest could be paid, at the) Tj T*
(option of the tenant, either in work or in money.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In this transitional form of agreement prevalent in 1882, the peasant) Tj T*
(appears, properly speaking, as tenant and laborer at once. The next) Tj T*
(step is toward the differentiation of both.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The purely money form of rent has already won the field over about one) Tj T*
(half of the whole area of rented land.) Tj T*
