(The amphibious character of the peasant, who is at once farmer and) Tj T*
(laborer, proves a very important factor in shaping the relations of) Tj T*
(Russian economic life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In Russia we have the case of the so called allotment system on a large) Tj T*
(scale. The influence of this system was picturesquely elucidated by) Tj T*
(John Stuart Mill when he stated that ?it makes the people grow their) Tj T*
(own poor rates.?[72] Exactly the same is observed in Russia.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The greater part of the work in agriculture, as well as in industry, is) Tj T*
(performed by farmers.[73] With them the earnings from outside labor are) Tj T*
(to cover only a part of their expenses, which cannot be provided for) Tj T*
(by farming. It is obvious that wages alone must fall below the usual) Tj T*
(standard of life.[74]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We have seen how, in the course of the evolution from farmer to wage) Tj T*
(worker, the tenant first becomes farm laborer. Accordingly it is) Tj T*
(natural to find farm labor prevailing among the local occupations of) Tj T*
(the peasants:) Tj T*
