(to that of agricultural labor. In many of the households in question) Tj T*
(there are, besides the artisan, other male members of the family who) Tj T*
(carry on their farming.[81] In fall and winter the farmer, who is at) Tj T*
(the same time an artisan, would work for any price. A tailor, _e. g._,) Tj T*
(travelling around his village, earns in the fall from 1.50 to 2.50 a) Tj T*
(week, while boarding with the customer. On the other hand, the maximum) Tj T*
(in wages is paid to carpenters, whose trade is carried on in the) Tj T*
(summer, so as to preclude competition on the part of the farmer.[82]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
