() Tj T*
(So long as the occupations of all the members of the family were) Tj T*
(identical, the tie of co-operation bound them closely together. The) Tj T*
(income of the family, due to their collective labor, constituted) Tj T*
(accordingly their collective property. The authority of the ?major? of) Tj T*
(the household was respected on the ground of his greater experience,) Tj T*
(which comes with age, as well as of his administrative ability.[96]) Tj T*
(When altered circumstances forced the family to look for its income to) Tj T*
(a variety of sources, the basis of the ancient household received a) Tj T*
(fatal shock. The carpenter who worked all through the summer in some) Tj T*
(far distant town was no longer an active member of the agricultural) Tj T*
(co-operative circle. On the other hand, his income being greater than) Tj T*
(that of his elder brother who was still employed as a farm laborer in) Tj T*
(the neighborhood, the spirit of individualism revolted against the old) Tj T*
(communistic rule. The age-long despotism of the elder over the younger) Tj T*
(members of the family became unendurable. The women, who had to suffer) Tj T*
(most, were the champions in this ?fight for individuality.?[97] The) Tj T*
(head of the family could oppose no moral authority to this spirit of) Tj T*
(?disregard of age,? inasmuch as, with all his agricultural experience,) Tj T*
(he had nothing to say in industry. Thus the growing economic) Tj T*
(differentiation within the family made its dissolution into separate) Tj T*
(couples unavoidable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
