(It might be supposed that landlessness was connected mainly with old) Tj T*
(age, widowhood, orphanry, and bodily defects \(blindness, lameness,) Tj T*
(_etc._\). Yet such, what we may call, biological phenomena will carry) Tj T*
(with them consequences that vary according to the social institutions) Tj T*
(of the time. The patriarchal family was not destroyed by the death) Tj T*
(of one of its male members. His widow and orphans belonged, in some) Tj T*
(analogy with the Roman family, not to the husband, but to the household) Tj T*
(as a whole. It was no unusual thing for a widowed daughter-in-law to) Tj T*
(be given in marriage to an outsider with the purpose of introducing a) Tj T*
(new male worker into the coöperative body in the place of the deceased) Tj T*
(member. Similarly the other members remained until death in their) Tj T*
(family. It was only after the dissolution of the patriarchal household) Tj T*
(that the feeble and helpless began to figure as a distinct group in) Tj T*
(village life.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the other hand the division of the original household and of its lot) Tj T*
(in the communal land necessarily resulted in a decrease of the live) Tj T*
(stock belonging to each family, and consequently in a decrease of its) Tj T*
(agricultural efficiency.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
