(The highest class in regard to the ownership of live stock is composed) Tj T*
(chiefly of the households of the old type that number at least three) Tj T*
(male workers, and whose shares in the communal land exceed the average.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The households of the new type consisting of two adult male workers are) Tj T*
(provided in the majority of cases with two working horses; but there is) Tj T*
(a very notable minority which is gradually falling into the lower group) Tj T*
(with only one working horse to a household.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Finally even that level appears to be too high for the households) Tj T*
(in which there is only one male worker. Only the minority of such) Tj T*
(households are in the position to keep up at least two working horses;) Tj T*
(the great majority have either one horse or none, and _vice versâ_: the) Tj T*
(groups with one horse or without horses are made up mainly of those) Tj T*
(households with only one adult male worker, their plots only very) Tj T*
(seldom exceeding the average, or even falling short of the average.) Tj T*
