112 0 obj
<< /Length 3614 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
() Tj T*
(Now, without a horse there can be no farming; and a household with only) Tj T*
(one horse is liable to go down in the long run.[101] Still these two) Tj T*
(groups cover at least one-half of the peasantry of to-day.[102] Thus) Tj T*
(the dissolution of the old peasant family sapped the productive forces) Tj T*
(of the peasantry at large and prompted the liquidation of independent) Tj T*
(farming with a considerable minority of the householders. A distinct) Tj T*
(group of the village is formed to-day by those peasants who for want) Tj T*
(of live stock with which to till their plots, are compelled either) Tj T*
(to hire their neighbors to do the work, or to lease their plots and) Tj T*
(consequently to stop their farming altogether. The bulk of this class) Tj T*
(is made up of those families in which there is only one adult male) Tj T*
(worker.[103] Lack of land, lack of live stock and lack of labor power,) Tj T*
(make it by no means an easy task for a ?singleton? to carry on farming,) Tj T*
(and a good many must needs fail.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It becomes plain that small peasant agriculture, based on the labor of) Tj T*
(the farmer alone, could stand only as long as its basis, the compound) Tj T*
(coöperative family, held together. The previous economic evolution has) Tj T*
(demonstrated that the co-operation of three adult workers is required) Tj T*
(upon an average to constitute a stable peasant household. As the) Tj T*
(progress of individualism will not stop in presence of the survivals) Tj T*
(of the patriarchal compound family, so the lacking labor force will) Tj T*
(have to be supplied by hire. The dissolution of the patriarchal family) Tj T*
(brings forth, of necessity, the employing farmer.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The characteristic feature of this class is that the employer is still) Tj T*
(the tiller of the soil. The laborer is hired only to help the farmer in) Tj T*
(his work, the average number of laborers employed varying between one) Tj T*
(and two to one household, so as to constitute the required coöperation) Tj T*
(of three working men.[104]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For the present this class appears but in small numbers in the Russian) Tj T*
(village,[105] and this obviously accounts for the little attention paid) Tj T*
(to the employing farmer in Russian literature, even in the statistical) Tj T*
(investigations. Still the need of hired labor increases on the larger) Tj T*
(farms[106] with the division of the compound family, as can be seen) Tj T*
(from the following table:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
