() Tj T*
(As the dissolution of the patriarchal family is going on at a) Tj T*
(progressive rate,[107] it follows that the class of employing) Tj T*
(farmers is on the rise. The farmer?s own family, supplemented by the) Tj T*
(assistance of one or two permanent wage-laborers, is the coming type of) Tj T*
(agricultural coöperation, which is destined to take the place of the) Tj T*
(natural family coöperation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER X.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE MODERN AGRICULTURAL CLASSES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The existence of the employer presupposes his correlative, the) Tj T*
(employee. Thus we are brought close to the fact that there have arisen) Tj T*
(opposite social classes within the village community.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It must be borne in mind, however, that the lines between the classes) Tj T*
(in the Russian village are as yet far from being as sharply drawn as) Tj T*
(in countries with developed capitalism. It would seem that laborers) Tj T*
(permanently employed outside of their farms must unquestionably be) Tj T*
(classed among the proletarians. And yet we find the majority of them) Tj T*
(maintaining the standard of farmers.[108] This is due to the existence) Tj T*
(of the compound family, the average household numbering two adult male) Tj T*
(workers, which enables one of them to carry on farming, while the) Tj T*
(other is employed outside.[109] Only the minority of the households in) Tj T*
(question that have only one adult worker, and accordingly we find that) Tj T*
(independent farming has been given up only by the minority of those) Tj T*
(householders who are permanently employed as farm laborers.[110] These) Tj T*
(are the genuine rural proletarians with whom the earnings from wage) Tj T*
(labor constitute the main source of income. Still they are landholders,) Tj T*
(and inasmuch as they have no live stock of their own, their plots are) Tj T*
(tilled chiefly by means of wage labor:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
