(Thus we have the very peculiar economic type of a wage-laborer who) Tj T*
(is at the same time employer of wage labor. It is obvious that the) Tj T*
(characteristics of a modern European proletarian could not properly be) Tj T*
(extended to the Russian agricultural laborer.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Class distinctions are very easily perceived, of course, when the) Tj T*
(classes have already ripened to a certain degree. In the embryonic) Tj T*
(stage, the true tendency of the development going on is disguised by) Tj T*
(the many transitional forms combining the characteristic features of) Tj T*
(opposite classes. The peasantist of ?the seventies,? whose opinions) Tj T*
(were influenced by European socialism, had no idea of class antagonism) Tj T*
(within the ranks of the peasantry themselves, regarding it as confined) Tj T*
(entirely to the ?exploiter?--_kulak_ or _miroyed_[111]--and his victim,) Tj T*
(the peasant imbued with the communistic spirit.[112]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The statisticians necessarily started in their investigations with) Tj T*
(preconceived ideas respecting the uniformity of the peasantry[113]) Tj T*
(as a class, except in so far as legal discriminations had to be) Tj T*
(taken into account. The study of the facts brought them subsequently) Tj T*
(to a recognition of the true position, and in some of the later) Tj T*
(_Reports_ attempts were made to arrange the data according to class) Tj T*
(distinctions. The main difficulty in the question is as to what) Tj T*
(proof should be selected for classification. The characteristics of) Tj T*
(employer and employee would cover only a minor part of the peasantry) Tj T*
(of to-day,[114] not to speak of a certain vagueness of the terms, as) Tj T*
(explained above. Mr. Shtcherbina, Superintendent of the Statistical) Tj T*
(Department of Voronezh, has classified the peasants according to: 1,) Tj T*
(the size of their farms, 2, the quantity of stock raised, 3, the number) Tj T*
(of adult male workers to a household, and 4, to the occupation by which) Tj T*
(they supplement the insufficient income derived from their plots. The) Tj T*
(households are accordingly scheduled into 320 minute sections, so as to) Tj T*
(afford the opportunity of subsequently combining them into wider social) Tj T*
(classes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We shall divide the peasantry into three main classes:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I. Those whose income from farming is sufficient to meet all the) Tj T*
(expenses of the household \(taxes included\), so as to obviate any need) Tj T*
(of wage earnings.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Households that pay their expenses by the income from commercial or) Tj T*
(industrial enterprises and draw a net profit from agriculture, are also) Tj T*
(included in that class.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(II. Farmers who are at the same time wage laborers, either in) Tj T*
(agriculture, or in industry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(III. Proletarians, _i. e._ those who stopped working on their plots and) Tj T*
