(    The antiquated presumption of the homogeneity of the village) Tj T*
(    found its practical expression in a scheme which came out of) Tj T*
(    the peasantist press, and caught the ear of the ruling classes.) Tj T*
(    This was the proposal to declare communal land inalienable.) Tj T*
(    The question at issue has had its history. So long as the) Tj T*
(    capitalized amortization tax exceeded the value of the land,) Tj T*
(    the number of peasants who had redeemed their lots in absolute) Tj T*
(    property was limited to a score of the wealthiest householders) Tj T*
(    in a district. It took about 20 years before the rise of) Tj T*
(    rent brought the price of land above the redemption debt, as) Tj T*
(    decreased by the previous amortization payments made by the) Tj T*
(    peasants. It then became profitable for speculators to advance) Tj T*
(    the money necessary for the repayment of the remainder, so as) Tj T*
(    to compel the community to carve out the lot into a separate) Tj T*
(    tract, and thus make the sale feasible. As this speculation) Tj T*
(    dates only from the eighties, the statistics gathered by local) Tj T*
(    investigations are as yet insufficient. The question can be) Tj T*
(    properly handled only when we have the data of a large region) Tj T*
(    comprising, at least, several _gubernias_. So the matter has) Tj T*
(    been dealt with in a series of articles in the Russian press.) Tj T*
(    It appears that a considerable number of peasant plots have) Tj T*
(    passed, by sale, into the hands of strangers, thanks to the law) Tj T*
(    permitting the alienation of communal land. \(Sec. 165 of the) Tj T*
(    General Statute of the Peasants freed from bond serfdom.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    To see our way clearly through the question at issue, we have) Tj T*
(    to discover who are the buyers of the land sold by the peasants.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    We have seen that only a minor portion of the quarterly lots) Tj T*
(    have been purchased by merchants. As a rule, the small lots) Tj T*
(    sold by the nobility are acquired by peasants only. \(_Cf._,) Tj T*
(    next chapter.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The question at issue is thus one that has been settled as) Tj T*
(    between peasants alone, and that affects neither the interests) Tj T*
(    of the nobility nor those of the capitalistic class. In such) Tj T*
(    cases it may well please the Russian government to throw a sop) Tj T*
(    to the peasantists. This _mésalliance_ of oriental paternalism) Tj T*
(    with some queer sort of state socialistic prohibitionism,) Tj T*
(    however, would be apt to meet with opposition from the very) Tj T*
(    ones who were supposed to be benefited.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    As the process of dissolution is obviously spreading from) Tj T*
(    within, and not from without the village, inalienability of) Tj T*
(    peasant land would simply mean gratuitous expropriation of the) Tj T*
(    poor for the benefit of the wealthy members of the community.) Tj T*
