(by the tenant for the benefit of the landlord. The area cultivated by) Tj T*
(the latter increased, diminishing the part of the estate rented to the) Tj T*
(peasant. Small peasant agriculture was being step by step displaced by) Tj T*
(large farming, and that continually without any additional investment) Tj T*
(of capital.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Finally, however, the displacement of the small farmer must needs have) Tj T*
(led to the gradual substitution of money economy for natural economy.) Tj T*
(As the number of impoverished peasants increased in inverse ratio to) Tj T*
(the tenant class, a time arrived when the demand for labor could no) Tj T*
(longer be supplied by tenants alone, and had to be provided for through) Tj T*
(wage labor. The employer became the creditor of the laborer. This) Tj T*
(necessitated money payments for the land given in tenure.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Such are the inferences necessarily following from the above review) Tj T*
(of peasant agriculture. The immediate study of agriculture on a large) Tj T*
(scale must obviously lead to the same conclusions.[155]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
