(To sum up, it is thanks solely to the obstinate persistence of backward) Tj T*
(methods in Russian agriculture that the nobility is able to maintain) Tj T*
(its position.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The biggest of the aristocratic landlords are the only ones who can) Tj T*
(keep on capitalizing a part of their net income.[175]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the whole, the existence of the nobility as an agricultural class is) Tj T*
(closely dependent upon the continued vegetation of a class of peasants,) Tj T*
(who are farmers and laborers at once, or who, to express it more) Tj T*
(accurately, are neither farmers nor laborers. We have seen what is the) Tj T*
(trend of the times with regard to this class of peasantry. The former) Tj T*
(masters will inevitably share the fate of their former serfs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER XIV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CONCLUSION: THE CONSEQUENCES OF THE FAMINE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The conclusions drawn from the previous discussion of the economic) Tj T*
(structure of the Russian village must be taken with a threefold) Tj T*
(limitation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the first place, the science of statistics is essentially a science) Tj T*
(of large numbers. There are many questions, by no means unimportant,) Tj T*
(which it has been impossible even to touch upon, their discussion being) Tj T*
(feasible only where large agricultural areas are concerned.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the second place, inasmuch as the facts and deductions have only a) Tj T*
(local basis, the question arises whether the conclusions drawn would) Tj T*
(also hold good when applied upon a larger scale.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the third place, the conditions prevailing some five or ten years) Tj T*
(ago must inevitably have undergone by this time great modifications.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is no exaggeration to say that the round thousand[176] communities) Tj T*
(in the section submitted to examination represent an equal number) Tj T*
(of varying combinations of the fundamental agencies of rural) Tj T*
(economy. Nevertheless, we observe a certain regularity as soon as) Tj T*
(a complex, sufficient and necessary, of units is taken as a basis) Tj T*
(for examination. Thus we notice that all the figures relating to the) Tj T*
(district of Ranenburg are copied with a remarkable constancy in the) Tj T*
(district of Dankoff in the _gubernia_ of Ryazañ. The same similitude is) Tj T*
(observed between the districts of Korotoyak and Nizhnedevitzk in the) Tj T*
(_gubernia_ of Voronezh. It points to a certain uniformity of economic) Tj T*
(constitution as prevailing under like conditions over a still wider) Tj T*
