(class.[189] The class of small farmers in Russia is evolving into) Tj T*
(a peasant _bourgeoisie_ similar to the French peasantry after the) Tj T*
(great Revolution, or to the American small employing farmers. The) Tj T*
(transitional groups of half farmers, half laborers, by whom the major) Tj T*
(part of the landlords? estates were formerly cultivated, have sunk) Tj T*
(through the famine into the proletarian class. The laborer having) Tj T*
(become a proletarian, it is by proletarian labor that the estates) Tj T*
(must be tilled, and agriculture upon a large scale becomes a regular) Tj T*
(capitalistic pursuit.[190] The nobility with its estates under mortgage) Tj T*
(can not possibly afford the capital needed.[191]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The land is destined to be divided between the large capitalist and the) Tj T*
(small farmer--the _homo novus_ of the village.[192]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus the present famine must be considered as a genuine turning-point) Tj T*
(in the economic history of Russia.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Family co-operation, village community, nobility, and natural) Tj T*
(economy--such was the economic constitution of Russia in the past.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Russia of the days to come will have for its basis a peasant) Tj T*
(_bourgeoisie_, a rural proletariat, and capitalistic agriculture.[193]) Tj T*
