(1. The community of former serfs of Mr. Balk, village and bailiwick) Tj T*
(Karpofka, district of Ranenburg: The arrears amount to 67.90 rubles) Tj T*
(from each householder. Out of the total number of 51 householders there) Tj T*
(are but 24 who cultivate their lots personally. Only three among them) Tj T*
(have two horses, the rest must do with one, and 26 \(one-half\) have) Tj T*
(no working animals at all. One householder among these 26 has a cow;) Tj T*
(the rest have neither horse nor cow. There are likewise only 13 cows) Tj T*
(to be distributed among the 24 better-off householders who personally) Tj T*
(cultivate their farms. Only one pig is raised in the village, and 87) Tj T*
(sheep--that is to say, less than two sheep, upon an average, to each) Tj T*
(household. This means that the peasants have no meat on their tables,) Tj T*
(and most of the children no milk. 10 ?householders? \(one-fifth of the) Tj T*
(village\) have neither houses nor land; they lease their lots in order) Tj T*
(to pay their taxes, and, in all probability, seeing the coincidence of) Tj T*
(the figures, they have no cattle either. The yield of rye is to the) Tj T*
(seed as 3 to 1, and that of oats as 2 to 1 \(_loc. cit._, Vol. II.,) Tj T*
(tables, pp. 56-61\). In 1864 many peasants? chattels in this village) Tj T*
(were sold for arrears. The majority of the peasants go a-begging \(App.,) Tj T*
(pp. 286-287\), and certainly are very little afraid of public sale for) Tj T*
(_où il n?y a rien, le roi perd son droit_. Neither is flogging endowed) Tj T*
(with any creative power. Yet, inasmuch as the community is responsible) Tj T*
(_in solido_ for the payment of the taxes, it was the minority who) Tj T*
(had to pay, in addition to their own arrears, those of the beggars.) Tj T*
