([187] The first chapters of this essay were written when the famine) Tj T*
(of 1891-92 had reached its climax. Now, while these concluding lines) Tj T*
(are being printed, the Russian papers have brought official reports) Tj T*
(of a failure in 11 _gubernias_, of which 5 are of the number of those) Tj T*
(affected by the last famine \(Voronezh, Kursk, Orel, Samara, Tula\). The) Tj T*
(_Zemstvos_ have applied to the government for appropriations for the) Tj T*
(next seed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([188] A delay in the payments was lately granted to the debtors of) Tj T*
(the Nobility?s Bank in the famine stricken region, for the purpose of) Tj T*
(saving numerous estates from being sacrificed at forced sale.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
